\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Description\b0{\*\bkmkstart description}{\*\bkmkend description}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 One-call orchestrator for new HPE ProLiant server deployments. Deploys a client-supplied ISO directly from a network share or HTTPS URL. Each step can be skipped with the -Skip* switches for re-running individual phases.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b Parameters\b0{\*\bkmkstart parameters}{\*\bkmkend parameters}\par
\par\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Parameter\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Description\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -ServerIdentifier\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Target server identifier (name, serial, OneView name, iLO IP, bay). Required.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -OneViewHost\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 OneView appliance hostname or IP.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -IloIp\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 iLO IPv4 address / hostname for the target server.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -ExpectedHostname\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Expected post-build hostname. Defaults to ServerIdentifier.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -Domain\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 AD domain to verify in post-build validation.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -SiteCode\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 ConfigMgr site code (e.g. P01).\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -ManagementPoint\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 FQDN of the ConfigMgr Management Point.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -DistributionPoint\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 FQDN of the ConfigMgr Distribution Point.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -SiteServer\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 FQDN of the ConfigMgr site server (for PSRemoting fallback).\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -BootImageName\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Name of the boot image to embed (e.g. 'WinPE x64 - HPE').\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -TaskSequenceName\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Optional task sequence name.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -ExternalIsoPath\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Path to a client-supplied ISO for deployment (skip build/publish). Resolved by the single shared Resolve-ExternalIsoPath helper. Accepts: - HTTP/HTTPS URL: Used directly (e.g. 'https://artifacts/win.iso') - NFS path: Used directly (e.g. 'nfs://server/export/win.iso') - UNC/SMB path (backslash): Converted to CIFS URL (e.g. '\\\\server\\share\\win.iso') - UNC/SMB path (forward slash): Same as above (e.g. '//server/share/win.iso') - CIFS/SMB URL: Used directly, round-trips the emitted URL (e.g. 'cifs://server/share/win.iso') - SMB URL alias: Normalised to cifs:// (e.g. 'smb://server/share/win.iso') - Mapped drive: Auto-resolved to its UNC share if mapped to a network drive (e.g. 'H:\\win.iso') - Local path: NOT supported - iLO cannot access local drives. Supply an SMB/UNC, CIFS/SMB URL, or HTTPS path instead. This module never creates SMB shares or requires Administrator privileges (regulated banking env). IMPORTANT - Local Drive Paths (e.g. 'H:\\windows.iso'): The iLO BMC cannot access local drives on the automation host. This module does NOT auto-create SMB shares and does NOT require Administrator privileges. Supply an already-shared path instead. When supplied, the ISO build/publish steps are skipped entirely. See ../PathParameterFormats.md for the full list of accepted formats.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -MonitorTimeoutSeconds\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Install monitor timeout (default 7200).\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -MonitorPollSeconds\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Install monitor poll interval (default 30).\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -DryRun\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Validate inputs and print plan without performing any destructive action.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -Force\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Required for the destructive Reset action (ForceRestart) issued by Invoke-IloRedfish. Refuses to proceed without this switch when the server's iLO reports power state On.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -InMaintenanceWindow\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Acknowledge that the target server is in an approved maintenance window. Required when -Force is not supplied and the server is currently On.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -OneViewMaintenanceMode\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Enable HPE OneView maintenance mode before destructive operations (ISO mount, reboot) and disable it after the build completes. Set to $false to skip maintenance mode orchestration (e.g. when OneView is unavailable or the server is not managed by OneView). Default is $true.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -AllowUnknownIsoUrl\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Skip the head-verify check on the ISO URL during pre-build validation (use only when the build pipeline runs offline).\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -GuardRail\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 MANDATORY safety gate for shared/production networks. A CASE-INSENSITIVE REGULAR EXPRESSION the resolved target server name must match before any destructive action. If it is OMITTED the command fails early with an expressive, logged error and performs no action. If it does NOT match the target, the build is aborted with no changes. When it matches, a destructive confirmation (typing YES) is still required unless -DryRun is supplied. Example (regex): -GuardRail 'quickview\\.ilo0' matches server 'quickview.ilo03.alp'. This prevents accidentally overwriting a production server when the client's test server lives on the production network.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -Json\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Emit the result as a JSON string on the success stream (for API integration / redirection) instead of the human-readable report. When omitted, the command writes a human-readable report to the host (terminal / transcript / logs) and does NOT dump a raw hashtable.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -PassThru\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Also return the structured [hashtable] result on the success stream. By default the command writes only the human-readable report and returns nothing, so the terminal/log never receives a truncated hashtable dump. Capture the result into a variable, e.g. {\f1 $r = Start-PhysicalServerBuild -PassThru\f0}, for scripting.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx2184\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 -Quiet\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Suppress the human-readable report (use with -PassThru / -Json when the caller handles display itself).\cell}\row\pard\sa120\par
